Firebase vs Firestore:
// Realtime Database: JSON tree
{ "users": { "alice": { "name": "Alice" } } }

// Firestore: collections + documents
// users/{userId} -> { name: "Alice", email: "..." }

// When to use Realtime DB:
// - Simple real-time sync (chat, presence)
// - Low latency, small data
// 
// When to use Firestore:
// - Complex queries, joins-like
// - Scalable, multi-region
// - Mobile/web apps

